  "observations": [
    "Mirrored/asymmetric incoming controls subtract their direction vector; detached incoming controls add their separate direction vector.",
    "Ellipse defaults origin to (0.5,0.5); its four cubic vertices use circleConstant 0.552284749831.",
    "PointsPath uses its world transform unless skinned; this increment rejects transformed skinned paths rather than discarding that contract.",
    "Rive documents procedural-to-detached conversion and animated vertex editing; Evir only converts static contour/vertex geometry and does not claim that animation support."
  ],
  "productChoices": [
    "Materialize supported static contour geometry into editable detached cubic controls.",
    "Preserve shape transforms, paints and supported skin/bone motion; reject contour/vertex key targets that cannot be represented.",
    "Keep read-only original viewing for unsupported structures; do not discard data bindings or additional contours."
  ]
